Use the official WBPSC website as the primary source for examination information:

https://psc.wb.gov.in/

Prioritize these materials:
- Official examination advertisements and notifications.
- Official scheme and syllabus documents.
- Official previous-year question papers.
- Official provisional and final answer keys.
- Official corrigenda and updated examination instructions.
- Officially published examination-related announcements.

The system must identify the examination cycle, advertisement number, publication date, and applicable version of the official scheme.

Before configuring a mock test, verify the current applicable:
- Examination stages.
- Total questions and marks.
- Subject-wise marks distribution.
- Duration.
- Question type.
- Negative marking.
- Syllabus.
- Language requirements.
- Any other relevant examination rules.

Never assume that a previous examination's pattern is automatically applicable to every future examination.

Store these rules in an editable, versioned examination-configuration database rather than hard-coding them throughout the application.

If the latest official information cannot be verified, clearly identify the uncertainty and use the most recent verified examination scheme as a provisional practice configuration. Do not present unverified rules as officially confirmed.

The system must keep historical examination patterns available so students can practice according to specific previous examination cycles.

