## 6. STRONG NON-REPETITION SYSTEM

This is one of the most important features of the application.

The student should receive a genuinely fresh mock test every time they start a new regular mock examination.

### Question history

Track:
- Every question presented to each student.
- The test in which it appeared.
- The date of the attempt.
- The student's selected answer.
- Whether the answer was correct.
- Time spent answering.
- Whether the student reviewed the explanation.
- The concepts associated with the question.

### Duplicate detection

Use unique question IDs and semantic similarity detection to identify both exact duplicates and substantially similar questions.

The duplicate-detection system must recognize when two questions differ only in wording, option order, superficial names, or insignificant numerical changes.

Maintain separate historical records for authentic PYQs, adapted questions, and AI-generated questions.

A regular mock test must exclude previously attempted question IDs and substantially duplicated questions from the student's history wherever sufficient alternatives exist.

### Fresh-test rules

When starting a new mock test:
- Retrieve unseen questions from the eligible question pool.
- Generate additional questions if necessary.
- Validate the questions before including them.
- Avoid repeating the same concepts in exactly the same way.
- Vary difficulty and topic coverage according to the examination blueprint.
- Keep the number of questions and section distribution consistent with the selected examination configuration.
- Remember which questions the student has already seen.

Previously answered questions may appear again in a separately labelled Revision or Mistake Practice mode because spaced repetition is useful for learning.

Do not mix revision questions into regular fresh mock tests unless the user explicitly enables that option.

The system must not promise literally infinite questions or absolute uniqueness. If the eligible pool is temporarily exhausted, generate and validate more questions. If sufficient fresh questions cannot be produced, clearly explain the limitation rather than silently repeating questions.

### Independent uniqueness levels

Offer three practice modes:
1. Fresh Mock Test — prioritize unseen questions.
2. Topic Practice — provide fresh questions for a selected topic.
3. Mistake Revision — revisit previous errors and closely related practice questions.

