### I. Part-II Preparation

Provide an optional module for the Conventional Type examination, based on the applicable official scheme.

Support the configured language requirements and relevant tasks, such as report drafting, précis or summary writing, and translation.

Use clearly labelled AI feedback, editable model answers, writing practice, and a teacher-review workflow where possible.

Do not apply Part-I MCQ scoring rules to Part-II written responses.

### J. Computer and Typing Practice

Provide optional elementary computer knowledge and typing practice modules to support preparation for the relevant subsequent assessment.

Clearly distinguish practice activities from any official assessment or qualifying rule.

