}

This is an illustrative response schema. Validate all generated data using strict application-side schemas before saving or displaying it.

Do not trust a model's self-reported verification status. Perform verification through separate application logic and reliable source data.

### AI reliability

Use appropriate timeouts, error handling, rate limits, and retries.

Prevent multiple identical generation requests from creating unnecessary duplicate jobs.

Cache reusable, verified explanations where appropriate.

Do not cache a student-specific explanation in a way that accidentally exposes another student's private information.

If a provider fails, explain the problem clearly and preserve the student's saved work.

Do not fabricate AI output or show a fake successful generation status.

